      ],
      "answer": "If validation checks fail during the Verdant Bay live patch window on 2026-03-24 from 02:00 to 04:00, an automatic rollback to the pre-patch ruleset is executed as per the playbook. The rollback procedure involves running the command `orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>`, which rehydrates the prior rules and replays the cache invalidation hook to restore the previous state. After rollback, the team notifies Verdant Bay, opens an incident for manual remediation, and reverts any partial replays of approvals. Before patching, a snapshot of OR-AUDIT-LOGS for the last 30 days is taken and saved to an evidence bucket to support compliance and troubleshooting. Validation jobs include running 50 synthetic approval flows and sampling 50 in-flight approvals marked by the customer; if any validation fails, rollback triggers automatically. The entire deployment is atomic with pre-checks and automatic rollback hooks to ensure safe reversion if needed [art_fff67d92fe41]. \n\nDetails such as step-by-step commands beyond the rollback CLI command, exact timing for rollback execution, or specific escalation protocols beyond notification and incident opening are not provided in the evidence.",
