      "answer": "Jin proposed a fast fix to avoid waiting on Okta change control by adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest that maps the SCIM attribute \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publishes a normalized field for the correlator. This is a configuration-only change that can be hot-reloaded with low risk, so it avoids the need to modify Okta flows directly. The mapping rule can be pushed as a hot-reloadable config change to the Signal Ingest pipeline, enabling normalization without appliance restarts during settlement windows. The timeline for pushing this mapping rule was set for 2026-03-20 EOD (AUS), aiming to quickly normalize attributes and reduce provisioning delays while waiting for the longer Okta change control process that could take 2 to 4 weeks [art_79f625aafa16, art_545110f843dc]. \n\nNo explicit command or detailed internal implementation of the mapping rule was provided in the evidence.",
